{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["The meaning of <b>and if it is on the bed</b> turns back to the object on which she sits. Now the object is on the bed, or object upon object; therefore the impurity is lighter. And Scripture did not mention a saddle (מרכב) for the woman, because Scripture speaks of what is common (בהמה) [n], and the ruling is the same."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The parenthetical (ס״א בהווה) indicates a variant reading in some witnesses: 'in the present/actual case,' contrasting with the reading (בהמ׳), i.e. 'בהמה' (beast/livestock). The implication is either that Scripture addresses the common case of riding animals, or the present case at hand. Translated both readings; retained the primary reading בהמה as 'what is common.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:20.419916978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}